{"change_summary":"Added canonical N/C/O2 budget plumbing to `tank_core`: `TankState` now exposes canonical `total_nitrogen()`, `total_carbon()`, and `budget_totals()` helpers backed by shared stoichiometry helpers in `types/budget.rs`, and `Engine` now supports optional per-tick budget tracking via `enable_budget_tracking()` / `budget_ledger()`. When enabled, the engine records per-action and per-system N/C/O2 deltas into a `BudgetLedger`/`TickBudgetRecord` history without allocating or recording anything on the default disabled path. Added integration coverage for helper completeness, 24-tick closed-system conservation, explicit water-change export accounting, and disabled-path behavior.","outstanding_risks":["Canonical live-biomass C/N totals still depend on shared stoichiometric helper assumptions in `types/budget.rs`; if future phases add new explicit element-bearing fields or refine biomass composition, those helpers and tests must be updated together.","The closed-system conservation checks use a quiescent no-growth scenario. Richer gameplay states may still expose pre-existing stoichiometry gaps in systems that do not yet move every element explicitly, but the new ledger will now make those imbalances inspectable.","The worktree also contains unrelated user changes outside this task in `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs`, `crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs`, and `.ralph-burning/`."],"steps":[{"description":"Audit the existing state layout and hourly/daily systems to identify every currently modeled N-, C-, and O2-bearing pool plus the engine stages that need per-tick attribution.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Implement canonical element-total helpers and shared stoichiometry utilities, then wire an optional `BudgetLedger` into `Engine` so queued actions and systems record per-stage budget deltas only when tracking is enabled.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Add budget-focused integration tests covering helper completeness, 24-tick closed-system N/C conservation, explicit water-change export attribution, and the disabled tracking path.","order":3,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Format and validate the change set against the broader `tank_core` test suite to catch regressions beyond the new ledger coverage.","order":4,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo test -p tank_core --test budget_tracking` passed (6 tests covering canonical totals, 24-tick conservation, water-change export attribution, and disabled-path gating).","`cargo test -p tank_core --test water_change_mass_balance` passed (8 tests), confirming the new engine instrumentation did not regress existing water-change behavior.","`cargo test -p tank_core` passed across the full `tank_core` suite." ]}